<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Falkirk (1298)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1298">1298</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Falkirk was fought on 22 July 1298, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-i-of-england">Edward I of England</a> defeated the Scottish army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-wallace">William Wallace</a>. English longbowmen and cavalry broke the Scottish schiltrons, the dense formations of spearmen that had to stand still to resist mounted attack. Wallace resigned as Guardian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> after the defeat, though resistance continued.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>William Wallace defeated an English army at the Battle of Stirling Bridge in 1297 but lost at <b>Falkirk</b> in 1298.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-scotland">Kingdom of Scotland · Military</a></li></ul></section>
